{
  "choices": [
    {
      "message": {
        "content": "{\n  \"chapter_id\": \"CH04\",\n  \"chapter_argument\": \"肠道微生物群干预（FMT、LBP、饮食）在增强实体瘤 ICI 疗效方面具备生物学合理性与初步临床信号，但临床可靠性受限于供体/菌株异质性、irAE 风险及缺乏 III 期确证数据。FMT 疗效高度依赖肿瘤类型与 ICI 方案背景，目前仅抗生素管理具备常规临床指导价值，其余干预需限定于临床试验。\",\n  \"units\": [\n    {\n      \"unit_id\": \"CH04_U01\",\n      \"focus\": \"FMT 在特定实体瘤中可恢复 ICI 敏感性，但疗效高度依赖肿瘤类型、ICI 方案背景及供体特征，目前仅处于概念验证阶段。\",\n      \"paragraph_tasks\": [\n        {\n          \"paragraph_id\": \"CH04_U01_P01\",\n          \"point\": \"NSCLC 单药背景下的阳性响应信号与安全性基线\",\n          \"development\": \"对比 FMT-LUMINate 试验中 NSCLC 队列的高 ORR（80%）与零 3 级 AE 数据，确立单药 ICI 骨架下 FMT 的安全窗口与潜在增效幅度。响应者获益主要依赖于基线有害细菌物种（如 Enterocloster、Clostridium）的大量丢失，而非供体菌株的成功定植。\",\n          \"source_uses\": [\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0583\",\n              \"role\": \"主论据\",\n              \"use\": \"提供 NSCLC 队列的 ORR（80%）及安全性数据（无 3 级 + AE），支持单药 ICI 背景下 FMT 的安全性与增效潜力。\"\n            }\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"paragraph_id\": \"CH04_U01_P02\",\n          \"point\": \"双免疫检查点阻断背景下的毒性放大与起病提前\",\n          \"development\": \"分析黑色素瘤队列中 65% 的 3 级以上 irAE 发生率及心肌炎病例，探讨双药骨架对肠道屏障破坏与系统性炎症的协同放大效应。部分严重 AEs 与富含 Prevotella 的供体有关，提示供体筛选的重要性。\",\n          \"source_uses\": [\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0583\",\n              \"role\": \"主论据\",\n              \"use\": \"提供黑色素瘤队列的毒性数据（65% 3 级 + irAE）及心肌炎病例，关联供体 Prevotella 丰度与安全性风险。\"\n            }\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"paragraph_id\": \"CH04_U01_P03\",\n          \"point\": \"耐药/进展队列中的阴性结果与生态位竞争\",\n          \"development\": \"结合 MITRIC 试验数据，说明在快速进展或高负荷耐药状态下，外源菌群定植失败（多为暂时性）与内源性抑制性网络（高 CD14+ 单核细胞、高 IL-8）占据主导，导致 FMT 难以逆转耐药。唯一获益患者的持久定植提示定植持久性与临床获益的潜在联系。\",\n          \"source_uses\": [\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0578\",\n              \"role\": \"主论据\",\n              \"use\": \"提供 MITRIC 试验的阴性疗效结果（ORR 0%）及转化医学发现，说明耐药状态下外源菌群定植失败与内源性抑制网络的主导作用。\"\n            }\n          ]\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"unit_id\": \"CH04_U02\",\n      \"focus\": \"定义明确的菌株联合体（LBP）在早期试验中显示改善生存趋势与免疫重塑潜力，但定植效率低、个体响应差异大，且商业混合益生菌可能无效甚至有害。\",\n      \"paragraph_tasks\": [\n        {\n          \"paragraph_id\": \"CH04_U02_P01\",\n          \"point\": \"CBM588 在 mRCC 中的阳性信号与机制假设\",\n          \"development\": \"展示 CBM588 联合双免疫的 ORR/PFS 数据，结合宏基因组中 Eubacterium siraeum 保护与 F/B 比率纠正，推导短链脂肪酸介导的免疫稳态恢复假说。该菌株在 mRCC 中显著改善中位 PFS（从 2.5 至 12.7 个月）。\",\n          \"source_uses\": [\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0143\",\n              \"role\": \"主论据\",\n              \"use\": \"提供 CBM588 在 mRCC 中的 PFS 数据（2.5 至 12.7 个月）及微生物组变化（E. siraeum 保护、F/B 比率纠正）。\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0596\",\n              \"role\": \"背景\",\n              \"use\": \"提供双歧杆菌在肿瘤治疗中的应用背景及机制见解，支持益生菌辅助 ICI 治疗的生物学合理性。\"\n            }\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"paragraph_id\": \"CH04_U02_P02\",\n          \"point\": \"MRx0518 在耐药队列中的安全性与初步 DCR\",\n          \"development\": \"报告 MRx0518 联合 PD-1 的安全性轮廓与 42% DCR，说明单株 LBP 在难治人群中的耐受性，但 PFS 较短（2.14 个月）提示单靶点激活（TLR5）不足以克服复杂耐药网络。ICI-refractory 患者中获益微弱（ORR 5%）。\",\n          \"source_uses\": [\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0125\",\n              \"role\": \"主论据\",\n              \"use\": \"提供 MRx0518 临床试验的设计与患者筛选标准，作为耐药性定义的参考。\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0230\",\n              \"role\": \"主论据\",\n              \"use\": \"提供 MRx0518 Phase I 研究的安全性信号与 DCR 数据（42%），说明单株 LBP 在难治人群中的耐受性与有限获益。\"\n            }\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"paragraph_id\": \"CH04_U02_P03\",\n          \"point\": \"商业益生菌的矛盾结果与定植困境\",\n          \"development\": \"对比 MET4 等联合体定植率低、代谢物改变仅见于亚组的现象，指出商业产品缺乏菌株活性保障与生态位竞争能力。观察性研究显示商业混合益生菌在黑色素瘤患者中与较差 ICI 预后相关（IFN-γ+ T 细胞频率降低）。\",\n          \"source_uses\": [\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0122\",\n              \"role\": \"例证\",\n              \"use\": \"提供 MET4 诱导宿主 IgG 反应的数据，揭示定植菌与免疫识别菌的不一致现象。\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0390\",\n              \"role\": \"比较\",\n              \"use\": \"提供观察性数据，显示商业混合益生菌在黑色素瘤患者中与较差 ICI 预后相关。\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0586\",\n              \"role\": \"背景\",\n              \"use\": \"提供 FMT-LUMINate 黑色素瘤队列的试验背景（Phase II），辅助对比 LBP 与 FMT 的试验设计差异。\"\n            }\n          ]\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"unit_id\": \"CH04_U03\",\n      \"focus\": \"饮食纤维与特定代谢物干预在观察性队列中与 ICI 疗效正相关，但随机对照证据匮乏，且代谢物补充面临药代动力学与肿瘤微环境浓度未知的瓶颈。\",\n      \"paragraph_tasks\": [\n        {\n          \"paragraph_id\": \"CH04_U03_P01\",\n          \"point\": \"高纤维饮食与代谢物升高的临床关联\",\n          \"development\": \"引用 P0401 队列数据，展示高纤维摄入如何同步提升粪便丙酸、富集 Ruminococcus 并上调肿瘤内适应性免疫基因，建立饮食 - 菌群 - 转录组的证据链。维生素 K 摄入亦独立关联于更好的 PFS（HR 0.60）。\",\n          \"source_uses\": [\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0401\",\n              \"role\": \"主论据\",\n              \"use\": \"提供高纤维饮食与粪便丙酸、肿瘤内免疫基因上调及 PFS 延长的关联数据。\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0155\",\n              \"role\": \"主论据\",\n              \"use\": \"提供 NSCLC 患者饮食模式与 ICI 结局的关联数据，特别是维生素 K 摄入与 PFS 的关系（HR 0.60）。\"\n            }\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"paragraph_id\": \"CH04_U03_P02\",\n          \"point\": \"饮食模式的荟萃分析与动物模型验证\",\n          \"development\": \"汇总 P0156 的 OR=5.79 合并效应量，结合禁食/高纤维动物模型中 SCFA 介导的抗肿瘤效应，论证饮食作为低成本辅助策略的生物学合理性。生酮及禁食模拟饮食在鼠模型中有效，但人类数据有限。\",\n          \"source_uses\": [\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0156\",\n              \"role\": \"主论据\",\n              \"use\": \"提供饮食干预与 ICI 结局关联的系统评价数据（OR=5.79），连接宏观饮食与微观微生物机制。\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0454\",\n              \"role\": \"背景\",\n              \"use\": \"提供不同饮食模式（植物基、生酮、禁食模拟）对微生物组及 ICI 疗效影响的结构化概述。\"\n            }\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"paragraph_id\": \"CH04_U03_P03\",\n          \"point\": \"代谢物补充的药代瓶颈与监测需求\",\n          \"development\": \"基于 P0473 综述，指出 SCFAs/肌苷等虽具明确受体靶点，但人体 TME 内浓度阈值不明，直接补充面临生物利用度挑战。三氯蔗糖等人工甜味剂可能通过耗竭产丁酸菌并干扰精氨酸/瓜氨酸代谢削弱 CD8+ T 细胞功能。\",\n          \"source_uses\": [\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0473\",\n              \"role\": \"例证\",\n              \"use\": \"提供 MaaT034 共培养微生物组疗法的临床前机制案例，展示代谢重塑增强 ICI 敏感性的潜力。\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0452\",\n              \"role\": \"局限\",\n              \"use\": \"阐述三氯蔗糖通过微生物组 - 代谢物轴削弱 T 细胞功能的机制，提示饮食成分的负面调节风险。\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0249\",\n              \"role\": \"例证\",\n              \"use\": \"提供黑覆盆子干预的探索性数据，展示从人体观察到人源动物模型验证的链条，但提示统计显著性临界。\"\n            }\n          ]\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"unit_id\": \"CH04_U04\",\n      \"focus\": \"当前微生物组干预的临床转化受限于供体/菌株异质性、irAE 风险交互及方法学不统一，需从经验性应用转向基于生物标志物的精准工程与标准化监管。\",\n      \"paragraph_tasks\": [\n        {\n          \"paragraph_id\": \"CH04_U04_P01\",\n          \"point\": \"证据阶梯与转化现状评估\",\n          \"development\": \"对比 FMT（概念验证）、LBP（早期信号）、饮食（观察性关联）的证据强度，明确当前仅抗生素管理具备常规临床指导价值。FMT 在难治性黑色素瘤中显示概念验证效力，但 LBPs 和 Consortia 仍处于早期阶段。\",\n          \"source_uses\": [\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0387\",\n              \"role\": \"主论据\",\n              \"use\": \"提供微生物治疗辅助剂（益生菌、菌群组合、FMT）的临床结局对比，揭示复杂性与治疗效果的相关性。\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0178\",\n              \"role\": \"主论据\",\n              \"use\": \"提供 FMT、LBP 和定义菌群的临床证据框架，分析影响干预效果的生态学和药理学因素。\"\n            }\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"paragraph_id\": \"CH04_U04_P02\",\n          \"point\": \"系统性障碍：监管、标准化与预处理的干扰\",\n          \"development\": \"剖析供体筛选缺失、制剂批次差异、万古霉素等预处理导致的定植失败案例，指出监管分类模糊阻碍了 LBP/FMT 的规模化审批。测序平台、生物信息学管道及样本采集方法的异质性导致跨研究结果不可比。\",\n          \"source_uses\": [\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0573\",\n              \"role\": \"背景\",\n              \"use\": \"提供优化 FMT 以增强 ICI 疗效的概念图，分类机制与临床挑战，支持标准化必要性的论述。\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0468\",\n              \"role\": \"背景\",\n              \"use\": \"提供微生物群对健康与疾病影响的背景信息，汇总方法学挑战和因果推断局限。\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0178\",\n              \"role\": \"主论据\",\n              \"use\": \"补充说明监管分类模糊及预处理（如抗生素）对定植失败的具体影响案例。\"\n            }\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"paragraph_id\": \"CH04_U04_P03\",\n          \"point\": \"未来路线图：多组学整合与大型 RCT 设计\",\n          \"development\": \"提出整合宏基因组/代谢组/AI 预测模型的精准分型策略，呼吁设计包含实时微生物监测、预设 irAE 管理预案的大型 III 期试验，推动从经验性补充向精准医学转变。分子病理流行病学（MPE）可指导个性化给药策略。\",\n          \"source_uses\": [\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0546\",\n              \"role\": \"发展\",\n              \"use\": \"提供调节 ICI 的微生物组机制全面框架，支持多组学整合与大型 RCT 设计的未来方向建议。\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0451\",\n              \"role\": \"发展\",\n              \"use\": \"提供利用微生物组进行癌症免疫治疗个性化医学的路线，支持精准分型策略与监测平台建议。\"\n            }\n          ]\n        }\n      ],\n      \"table_tasks\": [\n        {\n          \"table_id\": \"CH04_U04_T01\",\n          \"purpose\": \"比较三类微生物组干预策略（FMT、LBP、饮食）的证据等级、临床信号与主要局限，辅助读者快速区分已验证信号与探索性策略。\",\n          \"columns\": [\n            \"干预类型\",\n            \"证据等级\",\n            \"关键临床信号\",\n            \"主要局限\"\n          ],\n          \"row_tasks\": [\n            {\n              \"content\": \"粪菌移植（FMT）：概念验证阶段，特定癌种（NSCLC/黑色素瘤）有阳性信号但毒性风险高。\",\n              \"source_uses\": [\n                {\n                  \"source_handle\": \"P0178\",\n                  \"role\": \"比较\",\n                  \"use\": \"提供 FMT 在难治性黑色素瘤中的概念验证效力及生态药理学限制。\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"source_handle\": \"P0546\",\n                  \"role\": \"比较\",\n                  \"use\": \"提供 FMT 临床疗效数据的证据等级评估（早期试验）。\"\n                }\n              ]\n            },\n            {\n              \"content\": \"活体生物药（LBP）：早期信号阶段，定植率低且单株激活不足以克服耐药。\",\n              \"source_uses\": [\n                {\n                  \"source_handle\": \"P0387\",\n                  \"role\": \"比较\",\n                  \"use\": \"提供 LBP 与 FMT 的复杂度对比及临床结局差异。\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"source_handle\": \"P0178\",\n                  \"role\": \"比较\",\n                  \"use\": \"提供 LBP 在特定癌种中的早期信号及批次一致性挑战。\"\n                }\n              ]\n            },\n            {\n              \"content\": \"饮食与代谢物：观察性关联为主，缺乏 RCT 确证，药代动力学瓶颈明显。\",\n              \"source_uses\": [\n                {\n                  \"source_handle\": \"P0546\",\n                  \"role\": \"比较\",\n                  \"use\": \"提供饮食干预的机制路径及异质性说明。\"\n                },\n                {\n                  \"source_handle\": \"P0387\",\n                  \"role\": \"比较\",\n                  \"use\": \"提供益生菌/饮食干预的临床证据强度对比。\"\n                }\n              ]\n            }\n          ]\n        }\n      ]\n    }\n  ]\n}",
        "reasoning_content": "The user wants me to act as a **Chapter Editor** for a review article chapter (CH04).\nMy task is to organize the writing tasks for this chapter based on the provided input data.\nI need to:\n1.  **Allocate all selected sources** (`sources`) to paragraph tasks or table tasks.\n2.  **Organize sources with only case-level uses** (none in this input, all seem to be paragraph uses already) into paragraphs or tables.\n3.  **Define paragraph tasks**: `point`, `development`, `source_uses` (role & use).\n4.  **Reference existing paragraph tasks**: I must use the `existing_paragraph_tasks` provided in the `units`. I need to ensure every `paragraph_id` from the input is referenced in my output. I can merge them or keep them as is, but I must cite the `paragraph_id` in the `source_briefs` (wait, the instruction says \"use `source_briefs` to cite `existing_paragraph_tasks`'s `paragraph_id`\" but the output schema provided in the prompt description says `paragraph_tasks` should have `paragraph_id`, `point`, `development`, `source_uses`. The instruction also says \"point/development can be omitted - program will fill back the responsible person's original text\". However, the output contract JSON schema shows `point` and `development` as fields in `paragraph_tasks`. I should follow the output contract schema but ensure I don't rewrite the scientific content if I can avoid it, or rather, I should align with the `existing_paragraph_tasks` content. Actually, the instruction says \"引用负责人原任务... point/development 可省略，程序会回填负责人原文\". But the JSON schema requires them. I will include them based on the `existing_paragraph_tasks` to ensure consistency, or leave them if the schema allows null (it doesn't explicitly say optional, but says \"can be omitted\"). Let's look at the \"Output Contract\" section: it shows `point` and `development` as strings. I will fill them based on the `existing_paragraph_tasks` to ensure the writer knows what to write, as I am arranging the tasks.\n    *Correction*: The instruction says \"每个段落任务写清：作者要表达的判断（point）、展开逻辑（development）...\". But also \"引用负责人原任务，不重写研究内容... point/development 可省略，程序会回填负责人原文\". This is slightly contradictory. Usually, if I am arranging tasks, I should keep the original `point` and `development` from `existing_paragraph_tasks` to ensure I don't change the science. I will copy them from `existing_paragraph_tasks` into my output `paragraph_tasks` for clarity, or if the system handles回填，I might just need to ensure the `paragraph_id` matches. However, the JSON schema requires `point` and `development`. I will populate them with the content from `existing_paragraph_tasks` to be safe and helpful for the writer.\n5.  **Ensure every `source_handle` is used**: I need to check the `sources` list and make sure every handle appears in `source_uses` of some paragraph or table, or in `unused_sources` with a reason.\n6.  **No new retrieval**: Use only provided info.\n7.  **Output format**: JSON object as specified.\n\n**Plan:**\n1.  **Review Units and Existing Paragraph Tasks**:\n    *   CH04_U01: P01, P02, P03. Sources: P0583 (P01, P02), P0578 (P03).\n    *   CH04_U02: P01, P02, P03. Sources: P0596, P0143 (P01); P0125, P0230 (P02); P0586, P0390, P0122 (P03).\n    *   CH04_U03: P01, P02, P03. Sources: P0401, P0155 (P01); P0156, P0454 (P02); P0473, P0452, P0249 (P03).\n    *   CH04_U04: P01, P02, P03. Sources: P0387, P0178 (P01); P0573, P0468, P0178 (P02); P0546, P0451 (P03).\n\n2.  **Check Source Allocation**:\n    *   P0122: U02_P03\n    *   P0125: U02_P02\n    *   P0143: U02_P01\n    *   P0155: U03_P01\n    *   P0156: U03_P02\n    *   P0178: U04_P01, U04_P02\n    *   P0230: U02_P02\n    *   P0249: U03_P03\n    *   P0387: U04_P01\n    *   P0390: U02_P03\n    *   P0401: U03_P01\n    *   P0451: U04_P03\n    *   P0452: U03_P03\n    *   P0454: U03_P02\n    *   P0468: U04_P02\n    *   P0473: U03_P03\n    *   P0546: U04_P03\n    *   P0573: U04_P02\n    *   P0578: U01_P03\n    *   P0583: U01_P01, U01_P02\n    *   P0586: U02_P03\n    *   P0596: U02_P01\n\n    All sources seem to be assigned in the `existing_paragraph_tasks`. I just need to structure them into the output JSON, ensuring the `source_uses` in my output reflects the `source_handles` from the `existing_paragraph_tasks` and adds the `role` and `use` description based on the `material_purpose` and `conditions` provided in `sources`.\n\n3.  **Refine Source Uses**:\n    For each paragraph task, I need to specify `source_uses` with `role` and `use`.\n    *   **U01_P01 (P0583)**: Role: Main Evidence. Use: Provide ORR (80%) and safety data (0 Grade 3+ AE) for NSCLC cohort.\n    *   **U01_P02 (P0583)**: Role: Main Evidence. Use: Provide toxicity data (65% Grade 3+ irAE) for Melanoma cohort, link to donor Prevotella.\n    *   **U01_P03 (P0578)**: Role: Main Evidence. Use: Provide negative results (ORR 0%) from MITRIC trial, discuss colonization failure.\n    *   **U02_P01 (P0596, P0143)**: P0596 (Background/Review), P0143 (Clinical Data). Use: P0143 for PFS data (2.5 to 12.7 months) and microbiome changes; P0596 for mechanistic background on Bifidobacterium.\n    *   **U02_P02 (P0125, P0230)**: Both are abstracts of the same trial (MRx0518). Role: Clinical Evidence. Use: Safety profile and DCR (42%), note limitations (Phase I, small n).\n    *   **U02_P03 (P0586, P0390, P0122)**: P0122 (MET4 immunogenicity), P0390 (Probiotics negative association), P0586 (FMT-LUMINate melanoma abstract - wait, P0583 is the main FMT-LUMINate paper. P0586 is an abstract of the same trial? P0583 is 2026 fulltext, P0586 is 2024 abstract. I should prioritize P0583 for clinical data. P0586 might be redundant if P0583 covers it. But P0586 is assigned to U02_P03 in input. I must use it. P0586 `current_uses` says U02_P03. P0583 `current_uses` says U01_P01, U01_P02. Okay, I will follow the input assignment. P0586 use: Phase II trial context for FMT+Ipi/Nivo. P0390 use: Observational data on probiotics/fiber. P0122 use: MET4 IgG response data.\n    *   **U03_P01 (P0401, P0155)**: P0401 (Abstract, Fiber/Propionate), P0155 (Fulltext, Diet patterns in NSCLC). Use: Link fiber to PFS and microbiome changes.\n    *   **U03_P02 (P0156, P0454)**: Both Reviews. Role: Background/Synthesis. Use: Meta-analysis data (OR=5.79) and preclinical validation.\n    *   **U03_P03 (P0473, P0452, P0249)**: P0473 (MaaT034 preclinical), P0452 (Sucralose review), P0249 (Black Raspberry abstract). Use: Discuss pharmacokinetic bottlenecks and specific dietary components.\n    *   **U04_P01 (P0387, P0178)**: Reviews. Role: Synthesis. Use: Evidence hierarchy (FMT vs LBP vs Diet).\n    *   **U04_P02 (P0573, P0468, P0178)**: Reviews. Role: Background/Challenges. Use: Standardization issues, regulatory hurdles.\n    *   **U04_P03 (P0546, P0451)**: Reviews. Role: Future Directions. Use: Multi-omics, RCT design recommendations.\n\n4.  **Check for Tables**:\n    The input doesn't explicitly demand tables, but Unit 2 (LBP/Probiotics) or Unit 4 (Comparison of interventions) might benefit from a comparison table.\n    Unit 4 compares FMT, LBP, Diet. A table could summarize Evidence Level, Key Trials, Limitations.\n    Let's create a table for Unit 4 to synthesize the comparison of the three intervention types.\n    Columns: Intervention Type, Evidence Level, Key Clinical Signal, Major Limitation.\n    Rows: FMT, LBP/Probiotics, Diet/Metabolites.\n    Sources for table: P0178, P0387, P0546 (Reviews summarizing these).\n    This helps organize the \"Evidence Staircase\" mentioned in U04_P01.\n    However, I need to make sure I don't double-count sources if I use them in paragraphs. The instruction says \"Same paper can be used in different paragraphs, but purpose must be different\". Using a review in a paragraph for text and in a table for summary is acceptable if the `use` is distinct (e.g., \"detailed discussion\" vs \"summary data\").\n    Actually, to keep it simple and ensure all sources are covered in paragraphs as per input `current_uses`, I will stick to paragraphs unless a table adds significant value without complicating source tracking. The input `existing_paragraph_tasks` already structures the flow well. I will add a table in Unit 4 to summarize the comparison as suggested by `thesis` (\"distinguish verified clinical signals...\").\n    Wait, I need to make sure I don't miss any source. If I move a source to a table, I must ensure it's tracked.\n    Let's keep sources in paragraphs as per `existing_paragraph_tasks` to minimize risk of missing them, and add a table that *references* these sources or uses the reviews again for the summary.\n    Actually, the instruction says \"Prioritize arranging all selected sources\". If I put them in paragraphs, that's fine. I will add a table in Unit 4 to synthesize the comparison, using the review sources (P0178, P0387, P0546) which are already in U04 paragraphs. I will list them in the table `source_uses` as well.\n\n5.  **Drafting the JSON**:\n    *   Iterate through Units.\n    *   For each `existing_paragraph_task`, create a `paragraph_task` with the same `paragraph_id`.\n    *   Fill `point` and `development` from the input `existing_paragraph_tasks`.\n    *   Fill `source_uses` based on `source_handles` in the input task, adding `role` and `use` derived from `sources` info.\n    *   Add a Table Task in Unit 4.\n    *   Verify all `source_handle`s from the input `sources` list are present in `source_uses` (paragraph or table).\n\n    **Source Verification List:**\n    P0122, P0125, P0143, P0155, P0156, P0178, P0230, P0249, P0387, P0390, P0401, P0451, P0452, P0454, P0468, P0473, P0546, P0573, P0578, P0583, P0586, P0596.\n    Total 22 sources.\n\n    **Mapping:**\n    U01_P01: P0583\n    U01_P02: P0583\n    U01_P03: P0578\n    U02_P01: P0596, P0143\n    U02_P02: P0125, P0230\n    U02_P03: P0586, P0390, P0122\n    U03_P01: P0401, P0155\n    U03_P02: P0156, P0454\n    U03_P03: P0473, P0452, P0249\n    U04_P01: P0387, P0178\n    U04_P02: P0573, P0468, P0178\n    U04_P03: P0546, P0451\n    Table U04_T01: P0178, P0387, P0546 (Re-use for summary)\n\n    All sources covered.\n\n    **Refining `source_uses` descriptions:**\n    Must be specific about what the source does in *that* paragraph.\n    Example: P0583 in U01_P01 -> \"Provide ORR (80%) and safety data for NSCLC cohort.\"\n    P0583 in U01_P02 -> \"Provide toxicity data (65% Grade 3+ irAE) for Melanoma cohort.\"\n\n    **Refining `point` and `development`:**\n    Copy from `existing_paragraph_tasks` to ensure fidelity.\n\n    **Table Construction:**\n    Unit 4, Table 1.\n    Purpose: Compare the three intervention modalities.\n    Columns: Intervention, Evidence Level, Clinical Signal, Limitation.\n    Rows: FMT, LBP/Probiotics, Diet.\n    Source Uses: P0178 (Framework), P0387 (Comparison), P0546 (Mechanisms/Design).\n\n    **Unused Sources:**\n    None, all are used.\n\n    **Open Questions:**\n    The input has `open_questions`. I don't need to output them, but I should ensure I don't claim they are answered. The `chapter_argument` should reflect the uncertainty.\n\n    **Chapter Argument:**\n    Summarize the thesis: Interventions show biological rationale but clinical reliability is limited by heterogeneity and lack of Phase III data. FMT context-dependent, Antibiotic management is standard, others experimental.\n\n    **Final Check:**\n    - JSON format.\n    - All handles accounted for.\n    - No new science invented.\n    - `paragraph_id` matches input.\n    - `point`/`development` align with input.\n\n    Let's assemble the JSON.\n    Note: The instruction says \"point/development can be omitted - program will fill back\". But the schema shows them. I will include them to be complete, copying from input.\n    Wait, one detail: \"引用负责人原任务... 用 source_briefs 引用 existing_paragraph_tasks 的 paragraph_id\".\n    The output schema provided in the prompt description for `paragraph_tasks` does *not* have a `source_briefs` field. It has `source_uses